  "holdout_metric": null,
  "surprise": "NoPE (rotary rotation of q and k removed from all six Peri-LN blocks, 4,800,000 params identical to 107) scored 559/505/576 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 107-claude's 582/571/608: exact means 546.67 vs 587.00, -40.3, every seed down (paired -23/-66/-32), inside the registered -60..+40 range but near its bottom (central -10). Discard. Two surprises. (1) Removing RoPE was a large systems win: 4716/4704/4706 pretraining steps vs 3264/3208/3277 (+44%, predicted +1-3%), and RL sampling 304-351 samples/s vs 194-249, so RL rounds took 201-229 s vs 266-322 s and totals were 1467/1406/1405 s vs 1946 (the fork's apply_rope is ~8 small strided ops per q and k per block, 12 calls per forward, and this launch-bound model pays for every one). The extra 44% steps bought no fit: final val loss 0.0825/0.0800/0.0848 vs 0.0822/0.0827/0.0836 (minima 0.0797/0.0767/0.0782, all rising into the endpoint), held-out greedy 0.982/0.983/0.978 vs 0.9815/0.977/0.9785, so a position-free model fits cap-6 Lean chains about as well as RoPE with no more sample efficiency. (2) The registered mechanism is not supported: the RL start was much worse, not better. Round-1 targets solved 556/568/464 vs 722/689/679, round-1 sample acc 0.232/0.248/0.139 vs 0.29 mean, L* 9/9/8 vs 10, even though round-1 parse failures were similar (11078/9519/15004 of 48,000, 24.7%, vs 12155/7575/17990, 26.2%). So NoPE samples parse as often but prove less at lengths 7+, i.e. the content-addressed-retrieval story did not transfer to unseen lengths; this matches 058's finding that a NoPE layer strengthened rather than weakened the cap-6 prior. RL recovered part of the gap (r4 solved 1014/959/998 vs 1089/1031/1083, mean +403 from r1 vs 107's +371) but not all; final eval greedy 0.987/0.986/0.992. Lesson for the loop: RoPE costs ~30% of pretraining wall-clock and ~35% of sampling throughput here, so a cheaper positional encoding that keeps RoPE's extrapolation behaviour (e.g. a fused/complex-multiply RoPE, or RoPE on fewer heads) could bank the steps without the NoPE penalty.",
